{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1116102-inspiration-torg-and-the-cyberpapacy","id":1116102,"title":"Inspiration-Torg, and the Cyberpapacy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-14T14:03:06-07:00","id":1116102,"title":"Inspiration-Torg, and the Cyberpapacy","content":"Well, it you haven't heard, Torg is a game where powerful rulers of alternate versions of Earth that work according to different genres invade Earth, and attempt to spin it to their own reality. I've probably overviewed it before, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> One of these rulers is Jean Marleux, the Pope of a version of Catholicism that's gone a bit...cyberpunk. As in, the more metal in your body, the holier you are, and the Internet is viewed as a form of Heaven on Earth. Magic exists in his world, but he hates it-because it's a form of paganism to him. In fact, he hates it so much, that using magic in the Cyberpapacy's territory has a chance to summon demons born of his hate and fear for things outside his control.<br /> <br /> Where this intersects with Demon is his 2E version's canniness-basically he's a lot smarter about his tech than in 1E, and its effect on society. So, he's way more intrusive, but also far more subtle. His invasion was literally unleashing an &quot;apocalypse&quot; of demons he forced a bunch of mages into summoning on France and Spain, then arriving as a &quot;savior&quot;. From there, he offered his miracles of universal cybernetic enhancement...neglecting to mention that all his cybernetics are linked to the GodNet unless hacked, and that the fun Piety Points system he's offering to especially devout believers has its most major secret achivements offered for helping the Church Police. Or joining them.<br /> <br /> That, my friend, is one hell of a Descent baddie-particularly combined with the fact he and his clergy can channel their faith into miracles-on-command, often the spontaneous repair of electrical grids or to make anointed templars superhumanly enhanced robots. It's even stated his ideal world would make humanity machines whose only desire is to serve his clockwork image of God.<br /> <br /> That sound you heard was a bunch of Saboteurs making Gadgets in unison.<br /> <br /> So, what do you think about making the Cyberpapacy a variant setting, or importing elements into Descent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 07-14-2017, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T16:43:35-07:00","id":1116156,"title":"","content":"Isn't this very similar to Altered State in the Storytellers Guide?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T17:53:34-07:00","id":1116177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1116102-inspiration-torg-and-the-cyberpapacy?p=1116156#post1116156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't this very similar to Altered State in the Storytellers Guide?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the Cyberpapacy is a lot more blatantly religious than Mechopolis, and it is assumed you are rebels.<br /> <br /> Also, more importantly, their technological revolution happened in the Dark Ages. Their society has not evolved socially since then. This is a place where fedualism is still the govermental style of choice. With all the intrigue that implies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}